 "hypothesis": "H66-1 (MGD-F, built GeoTIFF): Blind hydrothermal fault conduits over-pressured in unmapped Great Basin valleys produce positive SiO2-chalcedony minus Na-K-Ca cation geothermometer disequilibrium (GDR #1391 wells/springs), 2-m temperature probe upflow plumes (F2mDAB), and Efimov airborne radiometric potassium hydrothermal alteration ridges (GeoDAWN K * K/(eTh * TC)), paired with tip-preserved lateral-flank shielding (r=2.5 px, H27_tip>=0.05) and 300 m (min_dist=3.0 px) score-ordered dot spacing. H66-2 (SGMC-REACT, Exp 3 screen): A substantial fraction of unmapped Quaternary faults are neotectonically reactivated pre-Quaternary bedrock faults recorded in USGS SGMC (1:500k) where 3DEP LiDAR scarps and GPS strain gradients confirm active slip.",
 "mechanism": "H66-1 adds 4 catalogue-free columns (H66_mgd_cat_excess, H66_mgd_chalc_excess, H66_spring_upflow_prox, H66_efimov_f_ridge) to the 82-column H35 RESMAG-TIP HGB detector, suppresses non-tip lateral flanks within 2.5 px of visible catalogue faults (preserving fault-tip relays where H27_tip >= 0.05), and thins at min_dist=3.0 px. H66-2 gates USGS SGMC bedrock fault proximity exp(-d_SGMC / 4 px) by 3DEP LiDAR scarp strike alignment/step (H66_sgmc_scarp_compat) and GPS 2nd-invariant strain * gravity THDR (H66_sgmc_strain_react).",
 "mimicking_non_fault_process": "H66-1 mimics: Stratabound lateral outflow plumes in permeable ash-flow tuffs/playa aquifers, agricultural/evaporitic brine mixing altering Na-K-Ca ratios, and potassic rhyolite domes/unwelded tuffs with primary high K/eTh ratios. H66-2 mimics: Inactive Mesozoic Sevier thrust ramps, caldera ring-fracture contacts, and compilation overlap between 1:500k state bedrock fault maps and USGS QFFDB.",
